(29) Concerning the contracts for the supply of electricity, hydrogen or natural gas under Article 2(4)(a) of REMIT, the key element of the geographical scope is that a delivery point of such electricity, hydrogen or natural gas must be in the EU.

(30) As a consequence, contracts for the supply of electricity, hydrogen or natural gas produced/generated in the EU but delivered outside of its borders will not be within the scope of REMIT, as they don't fulfil the criteria included in the definition of wholesale energy products under Article 2(4)(a) of REMIT.

